# EtClubBadge Component

## Purpose & Scope

`EtClubBadge` is a brand-fixed pill badge for the eToro Club program. Three orthogonal props produce the variants:

- **`variant`** — `legacy` (default) or `v2` (Club 2.0 wordmark). Prefer {@link ClubBadge} from `@etoro/features/club/rn` in Club surfaces so the experiment picks the variant.
- **`showLock`** — toggles the lock-icon prefix. Without lock identifies a Club entity (member, item); with lock flags Club-gated content (teaser cards, blurred values).
- **`colorScheme`** — pins the badge to a fixed appearance instead of adapting to the active theme. Useful on surfaces whose color isn't theme-driven (always-dark hero cards, fixed-color banners).

The badge is intentionally **brand-fixed**:

- The label is always the Club **wordmark** (`v2`) or literal `"Club"` (`legacy`) — not exposed via `children`, not threaded through i18n
- The icon is always `lock-fill` (when shown) — not configurable
- **`legacy`** — primary brand border (`colors.primary600`); lock + label use the carbon palette per `colorScheme`
- **`v2`** — carbon border; serif wordmark + lock use the carbon palette per `colorScheme` (see [Design Tokens](#design-tokens))

If your design calls for a different label, icon, or color, you want `EtBadge`, not `EtClubBadge`.

## Entry Point & Contract

```tsx
<EtClubBadge
  variant?: 'legacy' | 'v2'       // default: 'legacy'
  showLock?: boolean              // default: false
  colorScheme?: 'light' | 'dark'  // default: undefined (adapts to theme)
  accessibilityLabel?: string     // default: "eToro Club member" | "eToro Club"
  testID?: string
/>
```

| Prop                 | Type                          | Default                                                      | Notes                                                                      |
| -------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `variant`            | `'legacy' \| 'v2'`            | `'legacy'`                                                   | Club 2.0 surfaces should use `ClubBadge` from club/rn instead of setting this manually. |
| `showLock`           | `boolean`                     | `false`                                                      | Toggles the lock-fill icon prefix                                          |
| `colorScheme`        | `'light' \| 'dark'` | —                                                            | Pin to one variant regardless of theme. Omit to adapt to the active theme. |
| `accessibilityLabel` | `string`            | `"eToro Club member"` (no lock) / `"eToro Club"` (with lock) | Announces the badge's _meaning_, not its literal "Lock, Club" composition  |
| `testID`             | `string`            | —                                                            | Forwarded to outer `<View>` wrapper                                        |

## Usage Patterns

### Marking a Club member (without lock — default)

```tsx
import { EtClubBadge } from 'etoro-ui';

<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 6 }}>
  <Avatar uri={user.avatar} />
  <EtText variant="body-base-medium">{user.displayName}</EtText>
  <EtClubBadge />
</View>;
```

### Gating a Club-only feature (with lock)

```tsx
<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 8 }}>
  <EtText variant="heading-base">Analyst Consensus</EtText>
  <EtClubBadge showLock />
</View>
```

### Inside an upsell banner

```tsx
<EtCard>
  <EtCard.Header>
    <EtClubBadge showLock />
    <EtText variant="heading-compact">Get full access</EtText>
  </EtCard.Header>
  <EtCard.Body>…</EtCard.Body>
</EtCard>
```

### Pinning to one variant on a fixed-color surface

Use `colorScheme` when the surface behind the badge doesn't follow the app theme — e.g. an always-dark hero card, a marketing banner with a fixed-color background, or a screenshot-friendly preview. The override changes border, foreground (lock + wordmark), and fill together.

```tsx
// Always-dark hero card — pin the badge to the dark variant so it
// reads the same in both light and dark mode.
<EtClubBadge showLock colorScheme="dark" />

// Always-light marketing banner.
<EtClubBadge colorScheme="light" />
```

## Anti-patterns

### Don't customize the label

```tsx
// BAD — EtClubBadge has no children / label prop
<EtClubBadge>Premium</EtClubBadge>

// BAD — won't compile
<EtClubBadge label="VIP" />
```

**Fix:** For arbitrary labels, use `EtBadge` instead:

```tsx
<EtBadge color="green">
  <EtBadge.Icon name="lock" />
  <EtBadge.Label>Premium</EtBadge.Label>
</EtBadge>
```

### Don't wrap in a `Pressable`

```tsx
// BAD — badge is not an interactive control
<Pressable onPress={openUpsell}>
  <EtClubBadge />
</Pressable>
```

**Fix:** Use a separate button / link adjacent to the badge:

```tsx
<View style={{ flexDirection: 'row', gap: 8 }}>
  <EtClubBadge />
  <EtLink onPress={openUpsell}>Join Club</EtLink>
</View>
```

### Don't override the color via `style`

```tsx
// BAD — bypasses brand color, breaks dark-mode behavior
<EtClubBadge style={{ borderColor: 'gold' }} />
```

The badge intentionally has no `style` prop. The visual identity is part of the brand.

## Design Tokens

Two token sets are in play, switched by the `colorScheme` prop:

### Adaptive (default — `colorScheme` omitted)

| Element          | Token                      | Light mode             | Dark mode                   |
| ---------------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------- |
| Border           | `colors.carbon900`         | `#1B1E21` (carbon 900) | `#FFFFFF` (white)           |
| Lock icon, wordmark | `colors.carbon900`      | `#1B1E21` (carbon 900) | `#FFFFFF` (white)           |
| Background       | `colors.carbon900Inverted` | `#FFFFFF` (white)      | `#1B1E21` (carbon 900)      |

### Pinned (`colorScheme="light"` / `colorScheme="dark"`)

| Element          | `colorScheme="light"`    | `colorScheme="dark"`     |
| ---------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------ |
| Border           | `colors.carbonStatic900` | `colors.carbonStatic050` |
| Lock icon, wordmark | `colors.carbonStatic900` | `colors.carbonStatic050` |
| Background       | `colors.carbonStatic050` | `colors.carbonStatic900` |

The pinned mode uses the **static** carbon tokens (`carbonStatic900` / `carbonStatic050`), which never flip with the theme — so a badge with `colorScheme="dark"` looks the same whether the app is in light or dark mode.

The fill is the _inverted_ (or static-inverted) carbon 900 token specifically so the badge sits flush against the surface behind it — it reads as a primary-outlined pill, not as a filled chip.

## Sizing Specs

| Property            | Value              | Source                                                              |
| ------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Border width        | 1.5px              | Figma node `4712:50905` border                                      |
| Border radius       | 20px               | Figma `rounded-[20px]`                                              |
| Height              | 18px               | Figma `h-[18px]`                                                    |
| Horizontal padding  | 3px left / 4px right | Figma `px-[5px]` on the badge root (tightened from spec) |
| Gap (icon ↔ wordmark) | 2px              | Figma `gap-[2px]`                                                   |
| Lock icon size      | 10px               | Figma node `4712:50906` (`lock-fill`)                               |
| Wordmark typography | 10px Playfair italic | Figma node `4847:14763` (`club wordmark`); `PlayfairDisplay-MediumItalic` substitutes Larken |
| Backdrop blur       | ~4px (intensity 8) | Figma `backdrop-blur-[4px]`                                          |

## Accessibility

- `accessibilityRole="text"` — announced as a single label, not as a button
- `accessibilityLabel` defaults to the semantic meaning (`"eToro Club"`) — the lock icon and "Club" label are _decorative framing_ for the Club concept, so they're marked `accessible={false}` / `importantForAccessibility="no-hide-descendants"` and not separately announced
- Override `accessibilityLabel` when context provides more meaning, e.g. `"eToro Club — required to view this section"`

## Dependencies & Edges

### Internal

- `Text` — renders the Club wordmark in `PlayfairDisplay-MediumItalic` (Larken substitute; loaded by the host app)
- `EtIconV2` — `lock-fill` icon
- `useEtoroTheme` — `carbon900` + `carbon900Inverted` (adaptive) and `carbonStatic900` + `carbonStatic050` (pinned) tokens

### Design-system primitives

- All carbon tokens live in V2 carbon tokens (`core/styles/colors/tokens/v2/carbon.ts`)
- `primary600` lives in `core/styles/colors/tokens/v2/primary-tokens.ts` — used by the `legacy` variant border; not used by `v2`
- Lock icon source: `components/et-icon-v2/ds-react/icons/lock-fill.tsx`

## Related Context

